    },
    {
      "id": "-7_aacX-CDc8Du2QtiA8H",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2046.2140552936507,
      "y": -653.4417536185239,
      "width": 994.6193237304688,
      "height": 575,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aJ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1727702496,
      "version": 1469,
      "versionNonce": 1984402709,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786539553593,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What are the ways to generate unique short url\n    1. Prefix of long url\n        - bad idea, can lead to lot of collisions\n\n    2. Random number generator: \n        If 1B (10^9) urls needs to be stored then max. 10chars (1Billion have 10 digits) \n        will be needed which is way longer. Instead we generate a random number and base62 encode it.\n            - as random number can repeat, need to lookup in db\n               until finds a unique number.\n\n    3. Hash the long url and encode it?\n        - Can use hash function like MD5 on long url and then base62 encode the hash value.\n        - again encoded url can lead more chars than decided length \n            of short url, so collision can happen while trimming it. \n\n    4. Use Counter instead of random number\n        - increment the counter -> base62 encoding (will not exceed the max. chars length allowed?)\n        - predictibility of counter can leads to security risks \n                    - can ask user not to share private url\n                    - rate limit\n    \n    5. Bijective function like sqids.org\n    ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What are the ways to generate unique short url\n    1. Prefix of long url\n        - bad idea, can lead to lot of collisions\n\n    2. Random number generator: \n        If 1B (10^9) urls needs to be stored then max. 10chars (1Billion have 10 digits) \n        will be needed which is way longer. Instead we generate a random number and base62 encode it.\n            - as random number can repeat, need to lookup in db\n               until finds a unique number.\n\n    3. Hash the long url and encode it?\n        - Can use hash function like MD5 on long url and then base62 encode the hash value.\n        - again encoded url can lead more chars than decided length \n            of short url, so collision can happen while trimming it. \n\n    4. Use Counter instead of random number\n        - increment the counter -> base62 encoding (will not exceed the max. chars length allowed?)\n        - predictibility of counter can leads to security risks \n                    - can ask user not to share private url\n                    - rate limit\n    \n    5. Bijective function like sqids.org\n    ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "GLeuUZ_KltArGMl8U4ERg",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2050.8606638759325,
      "y": -902.4718515983886,
      "width": 368.13836669921875,
      "height": 167.50857987435592,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aL",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 954956832,
      "version": 1137,
      "versionNonce": 924723829,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786539553593,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Short Url Length\n    - 5 to 7 chars\n    - Base 62 (a-z, A-Z, 0-9)\n\nTotal combination\n    1. With 5 chars = 62^5 ~ 1 billion\n    2. With 6 chars = 62^6 ~ 62 billion ",
      "fontSize": 19.14383769992639,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Short Url Length\n    - 5 to 7 chars\n    - Base 62 (a-z, A-Z, 0-9)\n\nTotal combination\n    1. With 5 chars = 62^5 ~ 1 billion\n    2. With 6 chars = 62^6 ~ 62 billion ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
